Subject: [PATCH] Accept unhashed libstd shared library

During cross compilation, the libstd shared library may not have a hash in its filename.
This patch allows the runtime to accept such unhashed libraries.

This patch was generated with the assistance of AI.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]

Signed-off-by: Jean-Marc BOUCHE <jean-marc.bouche@foss.st.com>

---
 evcxr/src/eval_context.rs | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/evcxr/src/eval_context.rs b/evcxr/src/eval_context.rs
index fe595be..51152e8 100644
--- a/evcxr/src/eval_context.rs
+++ b/evcxr/src/eval_context.rs
@@ -2144,6 +2144,14 @@ fn std_lib_path(rustc: &Path) -> Result<PathBuf> {
             return Ok(entry.path());
         }
     }
+    let std_lib = Path::new(libdir.trim()).join(format!(
+        "{}std.{}",
+        crate::module::shared_object_prefix(),
+        crate::module::shared_object_extension()
+    ));
+    if std_lib.is_file() {
+        return Ok(std_lib);
+    }
     anyhow::bail!("No libstd found in {libdir}");
 }
 
